2. Definitions

"SDS Software" means the Sustainability Data Space software materials covered by
section 1.

"Evaluation" means non-production technical review, installation, execution,
testing, security review, audit support, compatibility checks, demonstrations,
benchmarks, and proofs of concept performed only to understand or assess SDS
Software. Evaluation must not deliver a service to third parties or support
ordinary business operations. Evaluation may use the included synthetic data or
other data the evaluator is lawfully entitled to use.

"Production Use" means use in ordinary business operations, delivery of a
service to internal or external users, processing operational customer or
third-party data as part of a service, making business/compliance/financial
decisions, operating a hosted or managed service, or otherwise using SDS
Software to obtain commercial, operational, or institutional benefit beyond
Evaluation.

"Commercial Use" includes selling, sublicensing, renting, leasing, providing
managed services, consulting or outsourcing services, SaaS, bureau services,
paid support based on SDS Software, or using SDS Software to provide products or
services to third parties.

3. Permission granted

Subject to this license, you may:

- view, download, clone, and fork this repository on GitHub;
- install and execute SDS Software in a non-production environment for
  Evaluation;
- create local copies, local builds, local virtual environments, local container
  images, and local test databases needed for Evaluation;
- run the included tests, examples, synthetic demo data, and documentation
  checks;
- make modifications only for Evaluation;
- maintain a public or private GitHub fork for Evaluation, provided the fork is
  marked as a fork or modified version, keeps this license, and keeps all
  copyright, attribution, funding, and third-party notices intact. A GitHub
  evaluation fork meeting these conditions is not by itself treated as a
  prohibited product or service offering;
- publish non-confidential evaluation findings, benchmarks, and review notes
  with truthful attribution, provided you do not disclose vulnerabilities
  publicly before responsible reporting and do not imply endorsement,
  certification, or production authorization;
- share issues and non-confidential evaluation feedback through GitHub Issues or
  another agreed channel;
- retain reasonable internal copies required for Evaluation auditability.

